  "notes": "BTL form 1500 (unemployment claim, 05.2026 edition), supplied by Shlomi on 2026-10-08 as T1500.pdf; PDF page 7 of 7 (pageIndex 6), printed 'עמוד 6 מתוך 6': section III (the employer's pay table, 24 months) and section IV (one-off payments and arrears included in the pay). Flat Word export with a text layer, no AcroForm, Letter page. The render is a 150 DPI pdftoppm render. Bounds are exact geometry: table cells are the white interiors between the painted #bfbfbf cell rules (pdf.js operator list), the comb comes from its black ticks, the underscore target from the pdf.js text run of the printed underscores. Conventions copied from btl-bl211-2015-page7 and btl-1500-2026-page5: an underscore run is a text target 11 pt tall above the printed line, x from first to last underscore; a ruled cell a person writes into is kind text (never table-cell), the whole white interior; a tick comb is ONE comb target with cells; a signature is a signature target above its line; the two date-range columns of section IV (from date, to date) are kind date; the month column and the in-month column are text, as the month column is in BL/211; a cell whose caption sits inside it (first name, family name) is the writing strip beneath the caption (btl-bl211-2015-page2 rule 3); table labels are the column caption, then the column group when there is one, then the row (שורה N), as the BL/211 pay table does. Pattern not covered by earlier truths: the row captioned סיבה אחרת לשינויים בשכר, whose four blank ruled cells are one free-text answer (see the note on that target). Not annotated: the section badges III and IV, the grey bars, the instruction text, the table header rows, the printed row numbers 1-24 (rightmost column of the pay table, pre-printed), the pre-printed X mark beside the signature caption, the page footer and the page counter.",
